/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - M-ary FSK sends k = log2 M bits by choosing one of M tones for a symbol time Ts = kTb.
   - The tones must be orthogonal over Ts: the spacing is 1/(2Ts) = Rs/2 for coherent detection and 1/Ts = Rs for non-coherent detection.
   - B ≈ M·Rs/2 (coherent), B ≈ M·Rs (non-coherent)
   - B is the occupied band in Hz.
   - Ps ≤ (M − 1)·Q(√(Es/N0))
   - the union bound for coherent orthogonal MFSK, with Es = kEb the symbol energy.
   - At a fixed Eb/N0 the error rate of orthogonal MFSK falls as M grows, because Es = kEb grows while the distance between any two tones stays √(2Es).
   - s(t) = I(t)cos(2πfc t) − Q(t)sin(2πfc t)
   - I and Q are the in-phase and quadrature amplitudes in volts, chosen from a set of levels each symbol.
   - In square M-QAM, I and Q are independent √M-level amplitudes.
*/
