/* book Worked example: Q: A 16-QAM link carries 20 Mb/s with rectangular pulses and Gray labels at Eb/N0 = 10 dB. Find the symbol rate, the null-to-null bandwidth and efficiency, the point that carries the bits 1011, and the symbol and bit error probabilities.
   1. k = log2 16 = 4, Rs = 20/4 = 5 Msymbol/s.
   2. B = 2Rs = 10 MHz; efficiency 20/10 = 2 b/s/Hz (= k/2).
   3. Bits 10 → I = +3a; bits 11 → Q = +a. The point is (3a, a), on the right edge, one row above the axis.
   4. Es/N0 = 4 × 10 = 40. Argument √(3 × 40/15) = √8 = 2.828.
   5. Ps ≈ 4(1 − ¼)Q(2.828) = 3 × 2.339 × 10−3 = 7.02 × 10−3; Pb ≈ 7.02 × 10−3/4 = 1.75 × 10−3.
   6. Check: QPSK at the same 10 dB has Pb = 3.87 × 10−6, so the doubled efficiency costs about 450 times the bit errors.
   Answer: Rs = 5 Msymbol/s, B = 10 MHz, 2 b/s/Hz; 1011 → (3a, a); Ps ≈ 7.0 × 10−3, Pb ≈ 1.75 × 10−3. */
