/* book Worked example 2: Q: An 8-FSK telemetry link sends 3 kb/s with coherent detection at Eb/N0 = 8 dB. Find the symbol rate, the tone spacing, the bandwidth and efficiency, and bound the symbol and bit error probabilities.
   1. k = 3, Rs = 1000 symbol/s, Ts = 1 ms.
   2. Coherent spacing 1/(2Ts) = 500 Hz; B ≈ M·Rs/2 = 8 × 500 = 4 kHz; efficiency 3/4 = 0.75 b/s/Hz.
   3. Eb/N0 = 100.8 = 6.31, so Es/N0 = 3 × 6.31 = 18.93 and √18.93 = 4.351.
   4. Q(4.351) = 6.78 × 10−6, so Ps ≤ 7 × 6.78 × 10−6 = 4.75 × 10−5.
   5. Pb = Ps × 4/7 ≤ 2.71 × 10−5.
   6. Check: binary coherent FSK at 8 dB gives Q(√6.31) = 6.0 × 10−3; going to M = 8 lowered the error rate more than 200 times while the band grew only from about 3 kHz (1.5 kHz spacing at 3 kbaud) to 4 kHz.
   Answer: Rs = 1 ksymbol/s, spacing 500 Hz, B ≈ 4 kHz, 0.75 b/s/Hz, Ps ≤ 4.75 × 10−5, Pb ≤ 2.71 × 10−5. */
