/* book exam traps: Bits per symbol are log2 M: 16-QAM carries 4 bits, not 16. | Square M-QAM has √M levels per axis: 64-QAM has 8 levels on I and 8 on Q, not 64 on one axis. | The QAM formula uses Es = kEb. Putting Eb in its place makes 16-QAM look 6 dB worse than it is. | MFSK bandwidth grows with M; it is the power-efficient scheme, not the bandwidth-efficient one. | Using Rs/2 (the baseband Nyquist minimum) as a passband null-to-null bandwidth gives an efficiency of 2k (8 b/s/Hz for 16-QAM) instead of k/2 (2 b/s/Hz). */
