/* book exam traps: MSK has h = 0.5. With h = 1 (spacing Rb) the tones are still orthogonal, but the phase moves ±π per bit and the spectrum is wider; that is ordinary continuous-phase FSK, not MSK. | Δf = Rb/4 is the deviation; Rb/2 is the spacing between the tones. | The Gaussian filter in GMSK comes before the modulator. Filtering after it would destroy the constant envelope. | A smaller BT narrows the spectrum; it does not raise the data rate or lower the error rate. It adds ISI. | MSK's main lobe (1.5Rb) is wider than QPSK's (Rb); its advantage is in the side lobes, not the main lobe. */
